--TEST--
A `spawn script` entry that names a method names a `static` one, because the script starts with no object to call it on — `rule:security/isolate-shares-nothing`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Job {
    public int $n = 7;

    public function run(): int {
        return $this->n;
    }

    public static function start(): int {
        return 3;
    }
}

// Compiles: `start` is static.
var $first = spawn script Job::start;

// Refused: `run` reads `$this`, and the script has no object for it.
var $second = spawn script Job::run;
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0802]: a `spawn script` entry is a path or a static method
   --> case.nvs:18:28
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
